  "body": "Found in the post-merge second safety read of PR #3225 (comment 7073688997). It gives no wrong output today.\n\n1. `crates/app/src/operation/wire_verify.rs`, `taper_chord`: on a model imported at reduced accuracy, the code widens the taper tolerance to the coarser mesh accuracy. That is the opposite of the rule of #864: a coarse model makes a check stricter, never looser.\n   - It has no effect today, because the post refuses each wire operation on a reduced-accuracy model (`fidelity_law.rs:234`, `model_fidelity/law.rs:53`).\n   - When #532 allows wire operations on such models, a gouge up to the coarse accuracy could pass. This must change before #532 merges.\n   - The function also reads only the source models, not the setup stock that the post-time refusal reads.\n2. On a model of unknown accuracy, the wire verdict line shows \"verify tolerance 1000000000000 mm\". The correct \"unknown accuracy\" refusal also blocks the post, so only the text is wrong.\n\nExpected: a coarse model never widens the taper tolerance. Add a test that fails when the widening comes back. Show the correct text for an unknown accuracy.\n\nThis issue is under the safety floor (a gouge check), so the effort is `effort:high`.\n",
